adjudication.rationale:
In `checkIfIsAvailable`, the new working-hours gate is:

```ts
if (workingHours.find(wh => {
  if (wh.days.includes(slotStartTime.day())) {
    const start = ...;
    const end = ...;
    if (start < wh.startTime || end > wh.endTime) return true;
  }
})) return false;
```

This rejects the slot if it is outside *any* working-hours entry that matches the weekday. With multiple working-hour ranges on the same day (e.g., 09:00–12:00 and 13:00–17:00), a 10:00 slot is inside the first range but outside the second, so `find` will return `true` on the second range and the slot is wrongly rejected. Correct logic should reject only if the slot is outside *all* applicable ranges (i.e., no range contains it).
